Highest-value simulation changes
1. Barometric altitude. `airDensity(airC)` uses only temperature with a fixed `rhoRef: 1.2` (src/drag/physics.ts:60, :34), and `conditionsForSeed` draws air, track, grip, wind and weather but no pressure (:84-89); `DragConditions` has no altitude field (src/drag/types.ts:35-42). Add a seeded baro/altitude term, fold it into `airDensity`/`conditionsAt` (:60, :66-74), show it in `conditionsText` (:64) and let RIVAL_TUNE's `rhoSpan` retune for it (src/drag/tune.ts:38, :123). Turn the new CONDITIONS.altitudeRange first, then RIVAL_TUNE.rhoSpan.
2. Fuel burn and changing mass. Mass is fixed on both sides of the line (`sp.mass + tu.ballast + DRAG.driver`, src/drag/physics.ts:212 and :268) and `staticRearShare` is fixed too (:57). Add a per-run fuel load that burns with work, so acceleration, aero drag and rear grip fall very slightly through a long run or a test session; a missing field can default to full and need no save migration. Turn the new fuel burn constant first, then `DRAG.driver` (:10).
3. Nitro that actually says what it does. The open note of ("nitro doesnt really add anything") has not been measured; instrument it where it lives: nitro is a latched flag (src/drag/physics.ts:184-185), `burn()` converts seconds by `shot / spec.nitroMax` (:123), and the torque gain is a flat `1 + tu.nitroShot` (:204), while the HUD shows only a seconds bar (src/drag/hud.ts:40). Give the bottle pressure/temperature and a tapered shot, put used seconds and peak gain in the timeslip (the `Timeslip` table stops at tyres, src/drag/page.ts:131, though `spin` already exists at src/drag/types.ts:90), and show the predicted with/without-nitro delta. Turn `LIMITS.nitroShot` first (src/drag/tune.ts:76), then the new pressure/taper constants.
4. Engine heat beyond boost. `Runner` already has `engineTemp`, `enginePeakTemp` and `retard` (src/drag/types.ts:86-87), but the only heater is boost charge (src/drag/physics.ts:199) and cooling is one exponential toward the air (:147). Add load/rpm/clutch-slip heating and slower coolant recovery so repeat burnouts, long boosted pulls and a hot day can retard timing without touching grip; the existing `boostRetardAt` (:50) and BOOST constants (src/drag/tune.ts:29-34) are the hook. Turn `BOOST.heatFade` first.
5. Throttle position and a real engine map. `DragInput.throttle` is a boolean (src/drag/types.ts:61), torque is the analytic `torqueShape` curve (src/drag/tune.ts:66-69), and the limiter hard-cuts torque (src/drag/physics.ts:194, :204); the pad already reports an analogue trigger in src/drag/page.ts:226. Add partial throttle, a named rev/torque map, a soft limiter and engine braking so launch modulation and late shifts have a physical cost. Turn `DRAG.rev` first (src/drag/physics.ts:14), then the new map constants.
6. Hand clutch modulation and honest controls. Engagement is automatic from one tune number (`engage = since / clutchBiteTime(tu)`, src/drag/physics.ts:187; src/drag/types.ts:21). Add a rebindable clutch action/axis in `DEFAULT_BINDS`/`BIND_GROUPS` (src/options/model.ts:16-29) driving slip and lock. While there, stop overloading one key: launch and shift are both `go` at src/drag/page.ts:224-226, Enter is reserved at src/options/model.ts:31, and burnout reuses `back` while the camera key silently toggles launch cam (:233). Give launch, burnout and launch cam their own actions; defaults stay in `DEFAULT_BINDS`.
7. Shift quality. A shift is a timer that snaps revs to wheel speed (src/drag/physics.ts:180-181; `wheelRpm` at :124), with time from `SHIFT_TIME` (src/drag/tune.ts:20, :58). Add torque interruption, lift-on/lift-off behaviour, rev matching and a missed-shift penalty when the clutch is hot or the tyres are spinning; the manual `shiftUp` action already exists (src/options/model.ts:18) and the HUD already prompts a shift (src/drag/hud.ts:62). Turn `SHIFT_TIME` first, then `CLUTCH.shiftTimeBonus` (src/drag/tune.ts:13).
8. Load-sensitive traction and lateral slip. Rear grip is a product including `r.rearShare` (src/drag/physics.ts:215), each wheel's force is split algebraically under a locked axle (:216-224), and yaw comes from torque bias, ruts and crosswind (:243-252). Add load-sensitive slip curves and lateral force saturation so weight transfer and a sideways car cost real distance; build on `SUSP` (:25-31) and `LANE` (:95). Turn `SUSP.spring` first, then `LANE.torqueBias`, `LANE.rubber` and `LANE.rut`.
9. Deep staging and rubber that persists. Rollout is one fixed distance/time (`DRAG.stageRollout`/`stageCreep`, src/drag/physics.ts:12, :97) and the lane's rubber/ruts are seeded waves rebuilt each race (:139-142). Let a driver deep-stage (shorter rollout, different R/T) and let burnouts and spins lay rubber on the strip for later runs in the same session; `rubber()` already feeds grip (:216). Turn `DRAG.stageRollout` first, then `DRAG.tyre.wearPerSlip` (:17) and `LANE.rubber` (:95).

Presentation and feedback
10. Show the realism already in state. The final timeslip stops at TYRES (src/drag/page.ts:131) but `Timeslip.spin` exists (src/drag/types.ts:90, src/drag/physics.ts:324); the HUD has no brake-fade, chute-open or rear-weight row though `brakeTemp`/`brakeFade`/`chuteOpen` (src/drag/types.ts:76) and `rearShare` (:83) are live. The tune screen also calls a perfect-driver run with auto shifts, warm tyres and no burnout a prediction (src/drag/physics.ts:327-329, src/drag/page.ts:69-73) without saying so. Add SPIN, BRAKE, CHUTE and REAR WEIGHT rows, and name the prediction's assumptions.
11. Make the live conditions and chute visible in both views. HUD and top-down show live weather (src/drag/hud.ts:65, src/drag/topdown.ts:57), but the 3D sign is built from the forecast once (src/drag/view3d.ts:108, :167); the chute is a boolean in 3D (:139) and a full ellipse in top-down (src/drag/topdown.ts:80) while physics ramps `chuteOpen` (src/drag/physics.ts:267). Refresh the sign, scale/fade the chute by its opening, and drift smoke/flags with `windAt` (:79). Top-down wheels are static rectangles (src/drag/topdown.ts:85-87), so add spin stripes too.

